{
"opening": "This release introduces several new features and critical bug fixes to the parsing library, enhancing its robustness with support for letters matching, result containment checks, and slice access. It also corrects issues related to hexadecimal parsing, case sensitivity in findall, and Fortran float handling.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m02",
"text": "The Parser must include a 'letters' matcher that matches alphabetic characters only, distinct from the 'w' pattern which includes numbers. The compile function should accept this new matcher type without raising errors."
},
{
"id": "m03",
"text": "Result instances must support the __contains__ operator to check if a specific value or key is present within the result. Match and Parser objects remain unaffected by this change but are part of the public interface context."
},
{
"id": "m05",
"text": "The Parser must raise an error if a part is not fully enclosed in matching braces during parsing. This ensures that malformed brace structures are rejected before processing."
},
{
"id": "m11",
"text": "FixedTzOffset must correctly handle timezone offset formatting as per Bug 92 requirements. Users should observe consistent behavior when parsing time strings with fixed offsets."
},
{
"id": "m15",
"text": "The Parser must correctly parse Fortran-formatted floating-point numbers. Invalid or unsupported formats should result in appropriate parsing failures."
},
{
"id": "m17",
"text": "The Parser must correctly identify and convert hexadecimal, binary, and octal numbers, including signed variants. The int_convert function must allow optional base arguments and automatically detect bases where specified."
},
{
"id": "m23",
"text": "The findall function must respect the case_sensitive parameter when searching for patterns. Case-insensitive searches should match regardless of letter casing unless explicitly overridden."
},
{
"id": "m25",
"text": "Left- and center-aligned searches must consume input up to the next space character. All listed public names must maintain their existing functionality while supporting these alignment behaviors."
},
{
"id": "m28",
"text": "Result instances must support slice access to retrieve subsets of matched values. Slicing operations should return valid Result objects or tuples depending on the slice bounds."
}
],
"closing": "Please ensure all public APIs behave as described above. Testing should verify both positive cases and error conditions for each requirement."
}
